WEBVTT

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.470
What's your name?

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.280
Ruon.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.920
That's everyone's name.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.590
That's not what I meant.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.470
But I...

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.170
Well, it's okay.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.030
Say, can we meet in 1.0?

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.940
In 1.0?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.890
That's right.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:48.800
No way.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.380
You say it so strongly.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.940
Are you a girl from a wealthy family?

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.300
You should just stay here forever.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.720
You should become 1.5.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.090
No way.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:00.880
Why?

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.230
Are you saying you can't forget this?

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.190
I have a lot of problems.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.700
Is 1.0 really so much fun?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.340
It's fun as it is.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.180
Hey.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.880
Let's meet in 1.0.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:19.750
No way.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.750
Definitely not.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.530
I'm going to sleep.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.330
Mimi, bring me some water.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.380
Yes.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.210
Here you go.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.270
I said water, right?

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:27.050
Vodka means water in Russian.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:29.850
And you prefer it this way, don't you?

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.330
That's right.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.510
So? Have you decided?

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.990
I was thinking it might be nice to go west.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.460
How many hiding places are there that I don't know about?

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.540
That's a secret.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.010
You're not cute at all.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.970
I came.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.390
Ruon?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.430
But you're...

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.410
I'm in 1.0 now.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.570
How can Ruon be in 1.0...

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.110
That hurts.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.030
What was that, geez?

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.090
Ruon!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.720
Oh, no!

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.260
You gotta be kidding!

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:54.810
Come out.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.320
I'll give you some tea.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.480
Um, what about the tea?

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.100
Suspects shouldn't make demands.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:11.660
T-That's...

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.360
Maeno...

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.620
Geez, what is it?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.730
Are you a student?

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:22.510
Excuse me.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.870
I'm from the Central Shinjuku Police.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.360
Did you see a suspicious young man around here?

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.070
Are you there?

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.410
This is bad.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:37.150
Am I being pursued by the police?

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:38.490
That's not it.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.080
That guy was a fake.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.810
How do you know?

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:44.890
Detectives work in pairs in situations like that.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.350
Also,

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:49.950
I know everyone in the Central Shinjuku Police.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.410
I'm a former detective.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:57.400
It seems I've become involved in something troublesome.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.870
So then, she's the only one I can depend on.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.050
Tamocchan.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.410
You've got a hobby of picking up boys?

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.050
Shut up!

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.250
He's a student at Tokyo Business University.

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:18.790
His name is Maeno Teruki.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.100
What is it?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.800
Is my face that unusual?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.850
Am I an endangered species?

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.430
Well, you might be close.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.940
Have we met before?

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.490
I wonder?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:38.520
And?

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.430
Ruon, eh?

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.880
It's true!

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.360
I wasn't mistaken!

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.660
Do you know how many hours you can stay in 2.0 each day?

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:52.990
About eight hours.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.380
I'm not 1.5!

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.670
I know about reality!

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.100
But a girl from 2.0 getting killed in 1.0...

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.170
It's not possible, is it?

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.630
That's why I was surprised.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.980
1.0 or 2.0 or whatever.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:11.540
There was always just one reality in the past.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:13.250
It's boring with just one.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:16.910
You can say that too.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.570
All you 1.5 people.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.070
Everyone blames it on the earthquake.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:33.700
Well, no one can say that 1.0 is better.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.880
Never mind that.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.590
What are you going to do about Ruon's murder?

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.040
What is it?

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.350
Don't you believe me?

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.190
We're not saying that we don't believe you.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.040
You know?

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:57.440
Even though you say a virtual idol was killed in 1.0...

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.240
You don't believe me after all.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.060
I believe you.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:05.150
At least, it's true that fake detectives are pursuing you.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:10.400
Maybe you saw something you shouldn't have?

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:13.130
Hey, Genta, move a bit.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:26.920
If I search for "Ruon," I get more hits than I want.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:28.860
Um...

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.920
Ruon was an avatar that appeared in 2.0 about five years ago.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.870
She was initially powered by AI,

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:39.940
but since there were no copyrights,
anyone could use her 3D data as an avatar.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.810
By the way, what do you use?

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:43.800
Me?

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.820
I made my own.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.310
This?

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.520
How did you...

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:52.780
Mimi's been using computers from before you were born.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:55.320
Impossible.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.730
Ruon's initial creator is unknown.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.320
Many people claim they created her,

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.330
but it's said that Kamiyama Katsuyuki did it.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:03.760
Kamiyama?

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.420
I've heard that name somewhere.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.100
Of course.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.150
The modern Von Neumann.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.930
You see his name in various places.

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:13.780
That's not it.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:19.650
I can't remember.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:22.280
He doesn't seem like someone I'd know.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.740
Hey, did you think about what I asked you earlier?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.780
I won't let anyone take care of me.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:31.950
Especially you.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.890
My, my.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:36.840
Even though I can manage one old man.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:40.750
Now then, should we go?

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:43.090
Go?

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:44.210
Where?

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:45.860
A good place.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:56.350
All right, I'm getting the hang of it.

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:56.800
Watch.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.280
All right.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.070
Is it okay?

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.160
It's all right.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:42.290
2015 was a good year for Burgundy.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:43.520
The body is firm—

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.240
That's not what I meant.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:49.260
Going to a batting cage and shopping and eating out, in broad daylight.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.220
What if those who are chasing me find us?

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.370
What if I say that's what I want?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.240
Seriously?

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:00.300
Looks delicious.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.300
Have you ever seen such a lame baggage carrier?

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.000
H-Hey, wai—

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.300
Wait!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.470
It seems desolate when we're off the main road.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:21.940
Are you still alive?

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.730
Geez.

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:29.730
Stigma?

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.250
You're so persistent.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.880
Well.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.640
I accepted this job.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.490
You're busy with business.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.120
You go back to the office.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.090
How much?

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:25.430
How much must I kill you before you'll die?

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.740
At least...

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.420
More than this.

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.400
As usual.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:38.550
I can't let my guard down with a woman like  you.

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:58.340
Not even this much, right?

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.860
Claymore mines didn't kill you either.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.780
Then, how about this?

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:11.760
Rin-san.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.050
This is bad.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:19.930
My control mechanism...

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:21.990
Damn it!

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:25.790
Damn it.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:32.520
Rin-san!

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.490
Teruki.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.170
Don't come any closer.

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:37.220
But...

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.030
Don't come any closer.

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:40.280
Please.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:44.870
Impossible...

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.550
At a place that exists somewhere in this world,

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.870
but is not part of this world,

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.350
there is Yggdrasill.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.980
It appears at its whim

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.230
and releases countless spores.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:08.140
Then, once in a million times, or once in a billion,

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:10.220
a special spore appears.

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.420
That is the Fruit of Immortality.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:16.110
In rare instances, people are able to touch it.

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:20.230
And then, they become immortal without realizing it.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.240
But that only applies to women.

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:26.030
Sometimes they're involved in an accident or something,

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:29.240
and then they realize they've become immortal.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:32.620
Just like us.

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.520
It's harder to believe it than not, right?

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.520
It's not like I'm asking him to believe it.

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:00.440
So who are we up against?

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:01.830
Did you figure something out?

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:02.880
There was someone else.

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:04.830
Apos' woman.

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:07.290
Eh? She's still alive?

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.530
Thanks to cyborg technology.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:13.700
That Kamiyama who made the avatar,

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.540
wasn't he involved in cyborg development too?

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:21.250
Speaking of that, it felt like she knew about Teruki.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.040
Something about "Stigma."

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:23.990
Stigma?

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.460
Energy and soul.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:28.810
Like the blood that flows from passionate believers.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.750
Sometimes called the Mark of God.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.290
The Mark of God?

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.900
I want something like that.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.320
Sometimes a large amount of information arrives,

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.520
and the server becomes overloaded.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:44.020
Does that happen a lot?

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.590
Quite a bit.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:50.740
It's said to be the aftershock from the net crisis of five years ago.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:00.040
Maybe I have to ask <i>her</i>.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.630
I thought you couldn't handle her?

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:04.220
I can't.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:08.670
Lately, you've been seeing her more than me.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.570
Be sure to lock this place.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:14.020
Also, shut off the gas valve.

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:16.420
Rin, you left it open last time too.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.320
Maybe I should take Teruki to my place?

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:20.560
Eh?

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:23.830
It's okay.

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:26.870
Right.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.820
You really can't die?

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:38.670
Yes.

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:41.440
What happens to guys?

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:43.530
Guys...

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:45.920
Yes.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.560
I'm doing somewhat better.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.450
Yes.

00:18:58.230 --> 00:18:58.930
No,

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:01.050
even I...

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.540
have times when things are rough.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.790
No! Please!

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:09.630
Yes.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:11.460
Yes,

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.710
I know.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:13.760
It's okay.

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:16.130
Yes.

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:17.510
Later.

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:33.670
What is it?

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:36.480
S-Stop it!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:39.750
I'm scared.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:43.120
Ruon, who's supposed to exist in 2.0, gets killed in reality,

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.020
and someone immortal appears right in front of me!

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.910
I'm an idiot, but I was a normal student.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:52.000
But why?

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.510
What should I do?

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.010
When I was small,

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:12.940
even before I went to elementary school,

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:15.760
I was in an accident once.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:22.250
I don't remember who saved me.

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:24.720
But,

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.750
she had the same scent as you.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:29.100
And the same warmth.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:32.240
Also, since when I was small,

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:34.360
I've felt that someone's been watching over me.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.330
It wasn't like someone had placed a guard on me.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.680
More like I was being protected.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.670
Say, that...

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:49.020
was you, right?

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:03.680
Good night.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.560
Asleep already?

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:47.280
You don't change.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.110
Small as usual.

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:51.560
You don't change either.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.180
It's not like that.

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:54.380
I'm already old.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.490
You don't change.

00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:58.740
You still like that grasshopper drink.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.310
You'd give that up for her.

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:05.160
How's she doing?

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:06.210
She's dead.

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:09.210
Really?

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:13.880
That's the usual fate for people like us who deal in underground information.

00:22:15.070 --> 00:22:17.300
You'll end up like that too, eventually.

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:19.200
Will you cry for me then?

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:20.350
Who would?

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.160
Never mind that, my information.

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:24.260
Okay, okay.

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:43.090
I heard she ran away?

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:45.320
This side is bigger.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:48.000
It must be difficult looking for her.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:52.600
I don't have time to deal with you now.

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:54.820
Please go back.

00:22:54.820 --> 00:22:57.970
She left her Stigma here, right?

00:22:58.590 --> 00:23:00.840
That's just a possibility.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:06.000
Someone on this side has made contact.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:07.460
Wh-Where?

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:09.960
She was badly damaged too.

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.120
I can't just let that slide for free.

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:17.480
Very well.

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:23.710
Kamiyama is definitely the one who made Ruon.

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:26.170
What bothers me is the project name.

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:27.250
What is it?

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:28.720
Project L'Isle-Adam.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:30.370
L'Isle-Adam?

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:32.350
A novel writer from long time ago.

00:23:32.350 --> 00:23:34.140
His most famous work was...

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:35.980
Don't tell me! That's what it is?

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.750
I'm just saying it's a possibility.

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:39.040
But...

00:23:42.170 --> 00:23:42.970
Yes.

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:44.470
Tamocchan?

00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:46.930
Digging through old materials,

00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:49.130
I finally remembered.

00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:52.070
Kamiyama Katsuyuki is Ruon's father.

00:23:52.570 --> 00:23:54.650
Kamiyama is Ruon's father?

00:23:54.650 --> 00:23:55.930
Impossible.

00:23:55.930 --> 00:23:57.810
Kamiyama is single,

00:23:57.810 --> 00:24:00.080
and there's no data on the net to suggest that.

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:02.950
There were various complicated circumstances.

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:05.200
Kamiyama acknowledged her,

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:07.820
but publicly the daughter doesn't exist.

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:10.200
Then, was she the person Teruki saw?

00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:12.150
No, definitely not.

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:14.960
Ruon will be sixteen years old forever.

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:18.090
She died, five years ago.

00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:20.670
And that was her father's fault too.

00:24:20.670 --> 00:24:22.600
Kamiyama killed Ruon?

00:24:24.340 --> 00:24:25.290
Yeah.

00:24:25.800 --> 00:24:28.310
One of my former subordinates was responsible for the case.

00:24:28.310 --> 00:24:32.820
He said he had positive evidence that Kamiyama was the killer, but...

00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:40.810
Be careful.

00:24:40.810 --> 00:24:43.960
He acts like a gentleman, but he can do terrible things.

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:46.090
What's the meaning of this?

00:24:46.090 --> 00:24:48.340
Ruon was killed by her father.

00:24:49.160 --> 00:24:50.210
It's mine.

00:24:51.300 --> 00:24:52.490
From my mom.

00:24:52.780 --> 00:24:54.200
Where are you?

00:24:54.200 --> 00:24:56.210
At a friend's place.

00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:57.460
Is that right?

00:24:57.960 --> 00:25:00.860
If you're staying over, at least please call me.

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:02.210
Sorry.

00:25:04.860 --> 00:25:06.510
Yeah, I know.

00:25:06.510 --> 00:25:08.470
The anniversary of my father's death is coming up.

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:12.660
Wait, don't hang up.

00:25:13.140 --> 00:25:14.700
Wh-Who is it?

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:15.360
Kamiyama Ruon.

00:25:17.540 --> 00:25:18.520
We don't have time.

00:25:18.520 --> 00:25:20.110
Please, let's meet in 2.0.

00:25:20.520 --> 00:25:21.470
Ruon?

00:25:24.210 --> 00:25:25.380
I-It's all right.

00:25:25.380 --> 00:25:26.120
Where are you?

00:25:26.120 --> 00:25:27.690
At the same server as before.

00:25:27.690 --> 00:25:29.130
Hey, wait!

00:25:38.330 --> 00:25:40.740
We have to immerse you.

00:25:40.740 --> 00:25:41.900
It's okay.

00:25:41.900 --> 00:25:43.990
We'll follow you.

00:25:43.990 --> 00:25:47.020
Even though I had to cobble together some parts really quickly.

00:25:47.340 --> 00:25:49.420
Is that right?

00:25:49.420 --> 00:25:51.180
You talk as if it's someone else's problem.

00:25:51.810 --> 00:25:52.900
You can say that too.

00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:17.500
Oh, no! We lost him!

00:26:21.590 --> 00:26:24.520
I've been following you forever.

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:25.560
We're finally alone.

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:27.480
Alone, you say...

00:26:29.010 --> 00:26:30.350
Don't worry.

00:26:30.350 --> 00:26:33.080
These are all images pretending to be human.

00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:35.380
They're protecting me.

00:26:35.380 --> 00:26:38.070
If they do that, I...

00:26:38.490 --> 00:26:39.540
Found him!

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:42.100
What's Teruki doing?

00:26:42.710 --> 00:26:45.140
Guys are sad.

00:26:45.140 --> 00:26:47.580
They get aroused even in situations like this.

00:26:48.270 --> 00:26:50.320
Who are you?

00:26:50.750 --> 00:26:53.250
Kamiyama Ruon's father killed her, right?

00:26:53.760 --> 00:26:56.130
My father is a scary person.

00:26:56.130 --> 00:26:58.610
He killed me for L'Isle-Adam.

00:27:00.270 --> 00:27:02.120
But I'm alive.

00:27:02.680 --> 00:27:03.710
What do you mean?

00:27:04.370 --> 00:27:05.590
What it means to be alive.

00:27:06.100 --> 00:27:08.000
What it means to meet you.

00:27:12.550 --> 00:27:13.600
It's my father.

00:27:18.410 --> 00:27:19.520
Impressive technique.

00:27:20.060 --> 00:27:21.730
Her protectors are being destroyed.

00:27:21.730 --> 00:27:24.010
Don't be impressed. Do something.

00:27:24.010 --> 00:27:25.520
I'm going to interfere.

00:27:31.940 --> 00:27:33.240
Wh-What is this?

00:27:55.650 --> 00:27:56.650
He broke through!

00:28:17.210 --> 00:28:17.910
Ruon...

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:32.620
Are you okay?

00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:34.720
I managed to break the connection somehow.

00:28:36.060 --> 00:28:37.610
We can't let our guard down.

00:29:03.170 --> 00:29:05.290
I guess we have to go to the resort.

00:29:05.290 --> 00:29:05.830
Yes.

00:29:08.850 --> 00:29:09.850
How are you?

00:29:10.390 --> 00:29:11.170
Are you okay?

00:29:11.170 --> 00:29:12.860
Y-Yes.

00:29:12.860 --> 00:29:13.960
I'm glad.

00:29:13.960 --> 00:29:17.060
But they traced where we were. That's not like you.

00:29:17.060 --> 00:29:19.370
I'm not that bad.

00:29:19.370 --> 00:29:20.820
Then, who did it?

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:24.160
Maybe the guy who saw you and the Stigma together.

00:29:24.160 --> 00:29:26.100
Apos and Kamiyama are connected?

00:29:26.100 --> 00:29:27.810
Stop that already.

00:29:28.390 --> 00:29:30.780
I don't know what's what anymore.

00:29:30.780 --> 00:29:32.320
What's happening?

00:29:33.720 --> 00:29:35.320
L'Isle-Adam.

00:29:36.020 --> 00:29:38.120
His most famous work is "Tomorrow's Eve."

00:29:38.650 --> 00:29:41.340
A story about creating artificial people.

00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:44.990
I said the first Ruon was powered by AI, right?

00:29:44.990 --> 00:29:48.830
Probably an attractor neural-network machine-learning program.

00:29:49.270 --> 00:29:53.560
What's with a name as long as a drunken old man's piss?

00:29:55.430 --> 00:29:57.680
Why are you laughing? You're such a sleaze.

00:29:57.680 --> 00:30:01.690
Attractors were proposed by a famous French mathematician,

00:30:01.690 --> 00:30:04.080
Jules Henri Poincare.

00:30:10.940 --> 00:30:11.690
It's nothing.

00:30:12.900 --> 00:30:14.160
To put it simply,

00:30:14.160 --> 00:30:16.410
it's a theory that when input values are within a certain range,

00:30:16.410 --> 00:30:19.700
the output values will also converge.

00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:22.380
That's pattern recognition?

00:30:22.380 --> 00:30:23.600
Huh?

00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:25.490
If you enter some dog-like values,

00:30:25.490 --> 00:30:27.200
the answer you get back will be "dog."

00:30:27.570 --> 00:30:29.120
That's how it is.

00:30:29.120 --> 00:30:34.210
An attractor neural network works a lot like the human brain.

00:30:34.730 --> 00:30:37.700
It's similar to the functioning of human pattern recognition.

00:30:37.700 --> 00:30:40.330
I don't really understand, but...

00:30:40.330 --> 00:30:43.220
Ruon is that attractor or something?

00:30:43.560 --> 00:30:44.600
That's right.

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:47.600
Inside the network, she continuously acquires new attractors,

00:30:48.030 --> 00:30:49.600
a machine learning program.

00:30:49.980 --> 00:30:52.180
That's "Tomorrow's Eve."

00:30:52.180 --> 00:30:53.620
But why is it in the net?

00:30:54.260 --> 00:30:55.940
It's probably a Turing Test.

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:58.370
You're using unintelligible terms again.

00:30:58.370 --> 00:31:01.020
An avatar that anyone can use in 2.0.

00:31:01.020 --> 00:31:03.950
If she blends in and you can't tell she's not human,

00:31:03.950 --> 00:31:06.250
that's a sign of advanced artificial intelligence.

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:12.130
Never mind that.

00:31:12.130 --> 00:31:14.970
I haven't seen any car for a while.

00:31:14.970 --> 00:31:16.020
For a while?

00:31:16.020 --> 00:31:16.380
Yeah.

00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:22.710
Get out!

00:31:32.930 --> 00:31:33.730
Rin-san!

00:31:44.320 --> 00:31:45.120
Hey!

00:32:14.320 --> 00:32:15.190
Are you done?

00:32:15.640 --> 00:32:17.500
I don't have time.

00:32:17.500 --> 00:32:19.040
I can't leave Ruon running around like that.

00:32:19.040 --> 00:32:21.890
Are you going to repeat what happened five years ago?

00:32:21.890 --> 00:32:24.780
Instead of the world, you should worry about yourself.

00:32:27.810 --> 00:32:28.610
Hello.

00:32:29.470 --> 00:32:32.040
Yes, my daughter is here.

00:32:32.040 --> 00:32:33.590
All I need is the Stigma.

00:32:34.770 --> 00:32:36.170
You got him?

00:32:37.030 --> 00:32:37.930
No.

00:32:37.930 --> 00:32:40.430
I didn't give an order like that.

00:32:41.450 --> 00:32:43.700
Yes. Anyway, bring him in immediately.

00:32:44.500 --> 00:32:45.650
Did you do that?!

00:32:46.530 --> 00:32:48.570
Your personality changes when you get mad.

00:32:49.670 --> 00:32:52.150
Don't move Ruon by yourself!

00:32:52.150 --> 00:32:55.300
There's no way I could do something like that.

00:32:58.010 --> 00:33:00.910
The site's in chaos. No one knows who's responsible.

00:33:01.830 --> 00:33:04.920
The culprit gave fake orders to close the road,

00:33:04.920 --> 00:33:07.820
and even dispatched the national military.

00:33:07.820 --> 00:33:11.010
Thanks to that, we're having a hard time here.

00:33:11.010 --> 00:33:12.950
Don't laugh.

00:33:12.950 --> 00:33:15.450
It's more difficult not to laugh.

00:33:18.850 --> 00:33:20.250
How is it?

00:33:20.850 --> 00:33:24.220
It's okay. I don't go for old men.

00:33:24.220 --> 00:33:25.310
Have you calmed down a bit?

00:33:25.790 --> 00:33:27.520
Yes, somehow.

00:33:27.520 --> 00:33:29.920
Sorry for intruding so suddenly.

00:33:29.920 --> 00:33:31.730
It's okay.

00:33:31.730 --> 00:33:35.740
I've known you since the great Mary Mama-san took care of me.

00:33:35.740 --> 00:33:37.820
Say, what's happening to our office?

00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:42.250
That... it's not sealed off or anything.

00:33:42.250 --> 00:33:46.300
The police and military are acting like nothing happened.

00:33:47.840 --> 00:33:49.910
Leave the police to me.

00:33:50.620 --> 00:33:53.280
I'll find Maeno's son.

00:33:53.280 --> 00:33:54.510
Don't try too hard.

00:33:54.510 --> 00:33:56.160
Our opponent can even move the military.

00:33:57.130 --> 00:33:58.630
Don't treat me like a fool.

00:33:58.630 --> 00:34:00.280
Even if I'm growing thin and old,

00:34:00.280 --> 00:34:03.980
I'm the man they called Daemon Yanagisawa at the Central Shinjuku office.

00:34:07.490 --> 00:34:08.640
Tamocchan.

00:34:10.400 --> 00:34:11.360
Genta!

00:34:11.360 --> 00:34:12.110
Hey!

00:34:12.770 --> 00:34:14.210
I know, I know.

00:34:14.210 --> 00:34:15.960
I'll give you some food now.

00:34:15.960 --> 00:34:17.890
I think Teruki is okay.

00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:22.400
They were only going after Teruki.

00:34:23.380 --> 00:34:25.070
I wonder if it's that Stigma thing?

00:34:35.220 --> 00:34:36.700
It really bothers me.

00:34:37.330 --> 00:34:39.000
When Teruki came in contact with her,

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:42.820
she looked like she was trying to suck him in, right?

00:34:42.820 --> 00:34:43.460
What about it?

00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:47.940
Artificial intelligence is a complicated program.

00:34:47.940 --> 00:34:51.890
A special hardware system would be the best way to implement it.

00:34:52.540 --> 00:34:56.890
So was that image downloaded from the special hardware?

00:34:57.500 --> 00:34:58.360
Yes.

00:34:59.800 --> 00:35:03.410
The most suitable hardware system to contain the software?

00:35:08.240 --> 00:35:11.700
Most likely, that was the murder Teruki first saw.

00:35:12.450 --> 00:35:14.320
An android.

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:17.300
Ruon ran away because she didn't like Kamiyama's place.

00:35:17.300 --> 00:35:19.500
And then, after being in contact with Teruki,

00:35:19.500 --> 00:35:21.930
she escaped to the net again.

00:35:21.930 --> 00:35:25.120
But she found out that she'd be sealed inside a physical body again.

00:35:25.120 --> 00:35:29.880
If that happened, how could she prevent Kamiyama from doing as he wished?

00:35:30.560 --> 00:35:33.650
By hiding the most important parts of her software elsewhere.

00:35:34.270 --> 00:35:35.480
Bingo.

00:35:35.480 --> 00:35:37.230
That's the Stigma.

00:35:37.230 --> 00:35:40.890
A nanodisk can store a hundred terabyte program.

00:35:44.990 --> 00:35:47.290
But to give something like that to Teruki...

00:35:50.560 --> 00:35:53.700
Ruon went to meet Teruki to tell him about it.

00:35:54.270 --> 00:35:57.170
And that's also why Kamiyama wants Teruki's body.

00:35:57.960 --> 00:35:59.410
Teruki's in danger.

00:36:03.220 --> 00:36:03.710
Tamocchan?

00:36:04.460 --> 00:36:05.240
Are you okay?

00:36:05.240 --> 00:36:06.960
Don't treat me like an old man.

00:36:07.550 --> 00:36:09.680
I figured out who abducted Maeno's son.

00:36:16.450 --> 00:36:17.110
Tamocchan?

00:36:18.330 --> 00:36:20.030
Tamocchan, what's wrong?

00:36:21.090 --> 00:36:23.100
Tamocchan, answer me.

00:36:23.710 --> 00:36:25.160
Code Red completed.

00:36:26.810 --> 00:36:29.110
Nobody ordered Code Red?

00:36:29.560 --> 00:36:30.490
Tamocchan?

00:36:30.490 --> 00:36:32.900
718 Express.

00:36:35.150 --> 00:36:37.320
Tamocchan, what's wrong?

00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:38.040
What happened?

00:36:38.040 --> 00:36:38.890
Rin.

00:36:39.970 --> 00:36:42.580
I got shot.

00:36:42.930 --> 00:36:44.270
Got shot?!

00:36:44.270 --> 00:36:45.400
Tamocchan, where are you?

00:36:45.400 --> 00:36:46.120
I'll be there right away.

00:36:46.120 --> 00:36:49.470
Rin, I...

00:36:49.470 --> 00:36:51.300
That time, you...

00:36:57.280 --> 00:36:58.180
Tamocchan!

00:37:03.890 --> 00:37:05.820
718 Express is a special flight

00:37:05.820 --> 00:37:08.070
that departs from Haneda Airport at 7pm.

00:37:08.590 --> 00:37:09.620
One hour from now.

00:37:09.620 --> 00:37:11.360
Please take care of Tamocchan.

00:38:13.890 --> 00:38:15.840
You're going to die.

00:38:16.310 --> 00:38:17.670
Where is Teruki?

00:38:17.670 --> 00:38:19.810
That little girl...

00:38:19.810 --> 00:38:21.720
Even though I gave her knowledge,

00:38:21.720 --> 00:38:25.240
even though I brought her to the frontiers of science...

00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:26.240
Where is Teruki?

00:38:26.650 --> 00:38:28.550
Just like her mother.

00:38:29.080 --> 00:38:31.950
Instead of staying by my side, she preferred freedom.

00:38:31.950 --> 00:38:33.630
She preferred the net.

00:38:35.380 --> 00:38:38.130
It's true that her basic personality is her own.

00:38:38.720 --> 00:38:42.040
But I made almost everything else.

00:38:42.040 --> 00:38:43.540
It's mine!

00:38:45.540 --> 00:38:49.250
Still, she acted as if she was human...

00:38:49.250 --> 00:38:51.340
and put everyone in danger.

00:38:51.340 --> 00:38:55.290
Because I gave her a body that lets her reach beyond the net,

00:38:55.290 --> 00:38:57.140
everything will end in destruction.

00:38:58.270 --> 00:39:00.440
She toyed with me!

00:39:00.770 --> 00:39:01.950
Where is Teruki?!

00:39:01.950 --> 00:39:06.670
That girl just wanted to use the Stigma for herself!

00:39:26.800 --> 00:39:28.680
Did I fail?

00:39:29.330 --> 00:39:32.510
Humans like you can't be stopped after all.

00:39:33.380 --> 00:39:36.040
It was you who ordered the military into action, not Kamiyama.

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:39.590
It was simple to give the order over the net.

00:39:39.590 --> 00:39:42.520
Any woman near Teruki should just die.

00:39:43.810 --> 00:39:45.140
Teruki...

00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:47.020
You're the one who said it.

00:39:47.020 --> 00:39:49.380
"Let's meet in 1.0."

00:39:49.380 --> 00:39:51.030
What are you?

00:39:51.610 --> 00:39:53.650
A program made by Kamiyama?

00:39:53.650 --> 00:39:56.560
Or are you the ghost of Ruon who died five years ago?

00:39:56.560 --> 00:39:58.570
Both.

00:39:58.570 --> 00:40:01.710
I was created to control this body.

00:40:01.710 --> 00:40:03.540
Using my data.

00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:10.160
Stigma is a program to suck in the data from your brain.

00:40:11.140 --> 00:40:14.210
He called it the frontier of science or whatever,

00:40:14.210 --> 00:40:16.040
but it's just murder.

00:40:16.040 --> 00:40:19.290
Suck up all the data and leave the body empty.

00:40:20.240 --> 00:40:22.230
But it's been fun.

00:40:22.230 --> 00:40:25.480
Everyone in 1.5 could play with me.

00:40:26.390 --> 00:40:28.260
But only Teruki

00:40:28.260 --> 00:40:30.390
ever asked to meet me in 1.0.

00:40:31.070 --> 00:40:33.680
Say, can we meet in 1.0?

00:40:34.710 --> 00:40:36.310
But it was impossible.

00:40:36.310 --> 00:40:38.060
Because I'm a program.

00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:41.570
Finally, I was given a body.

00:40:42.990 --> 00:40:44.460
I ran away immediately,

00:40:44.460 --> 00:40:46.010
so that I could meet Teruki.

00:40:46.450 --> 00:40:48.240
But Kamiyama's underlings followed me.

00:40:48.920 --> 00:40:51.620
That's why I passed the Stigma to Teruki and ran away to the net.

00:40:53.030 --> 00:40:56.290
Since then, I've been watching Teruki from the net.

00:40:56.290 --> 00:40:58.420
I was happy just to do that.

00:40:59.210 --> 00:41:00.810
If only you hadn't been there!

00:41:03.600 --> 00:41:07.160
Kamiyama thought it was good that Teruki had the Stigma,

00:41:07.160 --> 00:41:09.780
and tried to suck in Teruki's data as well.

00:41:09.780 --> 00:41:11.300
That's no good.

00:41:11.910 --> 00:41:13.810
I'm going to take him there.

00:41:14.600 --> 00:41:18.100
I came to 1.0 to be connected to you.

00:41:18.590 --> 00:41:20.330
So it's your turn this time.

00:41:22.750 --> 00:41:25.430
I don't need this airplane anymore.

00:41:25.430 --> 00:41:27.820
No, I don't even need 1.0 anymore.

00:41:28.510 --> 00:41:31.320
Let's go to 2.0 together!

00:41:43.330 --> 00:41:43.950
Teruki.

00:41:45.340 --> 00:41:46.420
Put that on.

00:41:46.420 --> 00:41:47.450
Okay.

00:41:47.450 --> 00:41:48.620
What about you?

00:41:48.620 --> 00:41:49.890
I...

00:41:50.600 --> 00:41:51.140
Get down!

00:41:53.170 --> 00:41:54.390
Teruki?

00:42:01.630 --> 00:42:02.790
Let go!

00:42:17.410 --> 00:42:18.330
You!

00:42:32.020 --> 00:42:34.050
This looks bad.

00:42:44.540 --> 00:42:45.160
Rin-san?

00:42:47.420 --> 00:42:49.220
Rin-san!

00:43:12.760 --> 00:43:13.710
Mimi...

00:45:03.030 --> 00:45:04.640
I was seeing a dream.
